---
// The site's icon links: the browser-tab favicon and the iOS home-screen icon.
//
// Its own component because `HeadExtras` composes sub-components and nothing
// else, and because these links have one shared concern — they are the only
// place the site's MARK appears outside the page body.
//
// The mark is the approved Harvard Alumni in Tech H lockup. Its geometry is
// shared with `src/components/BrandMark.astro`, which renders the same path in
// the header; `public/favicon.svg` holds the second copy because an external
// favicon file cannot import anything, and a test pins the two together.
//
// WHY A RASTER FALLBACK IS DECLARED AT ALL, when the SVG is better in every way
// a browser that supports it: a browser that does NOT use SVG favicons — and
// Google's search-result crawler — ignores the SVG entirely and issues an
// implicit `GET /favicon.ico` against the ORIGIN ROOT. On the project-subpath
// deploy (codeyam-ai.github.io/harvardintech/) that path is outside the site's
// base altogether, so it 404s and the tab falls back to a generic globe with no
// error reported anywhere. The implicit request cannot be base-corrected, so a
// root `favicon.ico` alone would still miss on the subpath deploy; declaring a
// PNG explicitly, through `withBase`, is what stops the request being made.
// (A root `favicon.ico` is shipped too, cheaply, for the custom-domain deploy
// and for crawlers that only ever ask for that path.)
//
// ORDER MATTERS: the PNG is declared first and the SVG second, so a browser
// that understands `image/svg+xml` still prefers the SVG — the type hint wins
// over document order — while one that does not takes the PNG rather than
// falling through.
//
// Every path goes through `withBase` so it resolves on the project-subpath
// deploy as well as on the bare domain.
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<link rel="icon" href={withBase('/favicon-32.png')} sizes="32x32" />
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={withBase('/favicon.svg')} />
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href={withBase('/apple-touch-icon.png')} />
